"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Preoperative PSA was elevated at 6.9. The surgical findings included a Gleason 3+3 (ISUP grade group 1), pT2 stage with no extraprostatic extension, positive surgical margins, and no seminal vesicle invasion. Absence of lymphovascular invasion was noted. A significant uncertainty arises from the lack of documented nodal status, as no lymph nodes were removed, and missing nodal sampling widens this uncertainty. Biopsy findings matched the prostatectomy specimen in terms of grade. Countervailing factors include the positive surgical margins and the preoperative PSA level. Information that would revise this prognosis significantly includes the postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory. The current uncertainty regarding nodal status is a key limitation. The fixed estimated horizon is 81.76 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 53.14–110.37 months; its coverage has not been validated."
